!|@0U92Friedrich Nietzsche 1844-1900|Y02000500|@CS03Maxims and Arrows|Y02000400
!|@BX0R1. Idleness is the begining of all
!|@BX12psychology. What? Could psychology|@BX1Dbe - a vice?
!|@BX1Z2. Even the bravest of us rarely|@BX2Ahas the courage for what he really
!|@BX2Lknows...|@BX373. To live alone one must be an
!|@BX3Ianimal or a god - says Aristotle.
!|@BX3TThere is yet a third case: one must|@BX44be both - a philosopher.
!|@BX4Q4. 'All truth is simple.' - Is that|@BX51not a compound lie?
!|@BX5N5. Once and for all, there is a |@BX5Ygreat deal I do not want to know.
!|@BX69Wisdom sets bounds even to know-|@BX6Kledge.
!|@BX766. Is it by being 'natural' that one
!|@BX7Hbest recovers from one's unnatural-
!|@BX7Sness, from one's spirituality...|@BX8E7. Which is it? Is man God's
!|@GF8Eonly |@BW8Pmistake or God only man's mistake?|c07|LAJ89AJ8O|LAJ89AU89
